description: Pagekit File-Specific Rules - Apply to specific file types. For PHP files: Convert implicit nullable parameters: $param = null → ?$param = null; Define explicit properties instead of dynamic creation; Use modern string function null checks; Replace deprecated Reflection methods; Use Symfony ErrorHandler for error handling. For JavaScript/Vue files: Use Vue.js 2.6 patterns and best practices; Follow UIkit 3.5 component structure; Always run yarn compile-js after changes; Only edit source files, never compiled bundles; Test frontend functionality after changes. For LESS/CSS files: Follow UIkit 3.5 naming conventions; Use consistent indentation; Avoid !important unless necessary. For JSON files: Maintain proper formatting; Validate syntax; Keep composer.json and package.json organized. For Markdown files: Use consistent heading structure; Update CHANGELOG-NEW.md with proper formatting; Keep documentation current and accurate
globs: *.php,*.js,*.vue,*.less,*.css,*.json,*.md
alwaysApply: false
